   121	### 1b. Opus-habit bank (default lever picks; 24 Oct second read of the 6 delivered tasks)
   122	Delivered scores are bimodal per lever: about 96 to 99 when the agent reads its main rule strictly and 41 to 72 when it does not. The misses that repeat across tasks are habits, not puzzles. Pick each lever's wrong reading from this list:
   123	- H1 lenient coercion: a quoted integer, a "12.0" or a padded string accepted where the rule says the field is a JSON integer (L5; collateral 37 pts).
   124	- H2 float rounding: binary float or half-up where the rule says exact decimal, half-even, at a stated step, with at least 3 planted ties (L8; pa M2).
   125	- H3 denominator scope: a share or rate divided by all rows where the governing file names a subset (L9; pa M1, 12 tests).
   126	- H4 normalisation in a rarely joined field (L10; slo D, 60 pts).
   127	- H5 make-it-match: a control fitted by a repair the rules forbid (L2).
   128	- H6 state consumed early: a cap or allowance used by an earlier record (L3).
   129	- H7 RETIRED 25 Oct (Ayush decision 3).
   130	- [v3: g1/C_18b5d99f.md:32, g1/C_3f39299a.md:45-46] H8 first fit: returns the first candidate that fits instead of checking that exactly one fits (S3).
   131	- [v3: g1 GS:5-10, g3/C_0b27b9dc.md:65] H9 shipped-only self-test: checks aggregates and invariants on shipped data, never builds an input that fires a stated branch (S2, S8, and the probe band).
   132	- [v3: CONFLICTS C11, g2 GS:26, g4 GS:36-42] Plain decoys, look-alike files, encodings, DST, duplicate ids and superseded notes are noise only. A partial-authority decoy (S5) is a lever.
   133	
   134	Habit levers leak by writing, not by data (metered probe 1: tests 199/199 with H1-H4 all held). Opus builds its own generator and tie fixture for every explicit sentence. A habit lever trips only when written like this:
   135	- H1: bare type property ("`units`: a JSON integer") beside a global trim or normalising rule. Never list the malformed values and never write a carve-out sentence naming the exception. precheck.sh fails LV-ENUM when a contract lists the malformed values of a typed field.
   136	- H2: only when the step or unit is stated once in a glossary and applied at a different stage (pa); otherwise graded noise.
   137	- H3: scope set by a defined term whose meaning differs from a per-line field the output already requires.
   138	- H4: only when the normalisation lives in one file's reading convention (slo); otherwise noise.
   139	- Stateful keys (H6, group counters keyed wider than the habit key) held as hidden-only cases are the strongest stated lever measured so far.
   140	- Opus's method (sentinel probe 1): it reads every rule file in one loop and transliterates each sentence using the per-line field the sentence names. Key the rule from a different file than the field it reads, and make the shipped control reconcile under both readings.
   141	
   142	Prefer levers that interact (one feeds the other): the biggest peer losses (127 to 205 pts) came from interacting levers.
