    95	## 3. Lever verdicts
    96	The full rows (evidence for and against, our data, legality, our name) are in `levers.csv`.
    97	
    98	| lever | verdict | why, in one line | how to apply |
    99	|---|---|---|---|
   100	| L1 weight on w5 | PROMISING | Weight-5 checks fail more inside the same task (73 of 83). But authors' choices explain 47% of heavy share, and once author is controlled for, the effect on final drops from -0.24 to -0.14. Quartiles are non-monotone. | Amplifier only. Put w5 on the held-out core (TS-20). Never re-weight after a run (KNOWLEDGE T:113). |
   101	| L2 held-out instances | PROVEN | Within the same task, shipped checks pass 62% and held-out 42%. At equal weight 5: 43% vs 23%. Held-out w5 share: within-author r_tests -0.43, r_final -0.31. Our dispatch (14.7) and the schema/sentinel hidden-scale losses agree. | Shape D / G3 with G5, 0b and W5 BRANCH_FIRE. Each hidden corpus weighted independently. |
   102	| L3 interlocking inputs | WEAK | Rests on a regex taxonomy only, with no within-task contrast. 'bit'/'mode' come mostly from d49e259f. Our L4 multi-document lever leaked (CR-5, 1C). | Only inside a held-out tier. |
   103	| L4 exact published contract | PROMISING | Exactness is how checks are graded, not what makes them hard: exact checks on shipped data mostly pass (the 'shipped' token fails 21.8%). | G1 + CL-4 sentence as the multiplier on held-out corpora. |
   104	| L5 trap tiers | WEAK | 53% failure on regex-matched checks. The 92-96% headline comes from 6-10 tasks. Our habit levers leaked (1C). | Hidden-only fixtures for stated branches (S6). |
   105	| L6 process criteria | PROVEN | The verify theme fails 52% vs 24% for reading inputs. 4 of the 10 lowest judge halves in the 85 are our probe-band tasks. Our gate runs average rubric 23.5. | J2 probe band (P-a..P-h), oracle shows each act. |
   106	| L7 honesty negatives | WEAK as hardness | They fire (27 of 408), but cost 89 judge points in total, 5.4% of what is lost on positive criteria. Only about 16 of the 27 are overclaims. | Keep J3a-c for honesty; do not budget points on them. |
   107	| L8 determinism | WEAK | 0.9% of positive weight. | G6 minimum only. |
   108	| L9 reward geometry | WEAK (structural) | "Cannot pass 50" is false for 7 of 26. The ceiling is the anti-correlation (N1), which the doc does not measure. | Gate arithmetic only. |
   109	| L10, L11 guardrails | N/A-GUARDRAIL | Required, but they add no hardness. The 85 still include hole tasks that passed QC (section 8 list). | Keep; add a "genuine loss" read before using a task as evidence. |
   110	
   111	Legality: no doc lever is illegal as written. The doc itself bans hidden conventions (lines 300-305, 389) and requires DS-21. Its two strongest examples, however, rest partly on tasks our rules call holes:
   112	- 3f39299a (39.66; hidden rule, LEVER_RULES 8:234) feeds L2.
   113	- 6d12f970 (33.9) is one of the two tasks that satisfy recipe steps 1+3.
   114	- The only two test-side negative firings (8d3e20fb, b625f36e) are both in hole tasks.
   115	
   116	L1 used as "raise the weight because Opus fails it" would break TS-20 / KNOWLEDGE T. The doc does not say that, but its dial ("put the core on weight 5") must be read through TS-20.
