   118	## 4. New lever candidates
   119	- **N1. Pair the two channels (held-out w5 tier + probe band).**
   120	  - Mechanism: across tasks the halves are anti-correlated (r = -0.40, -0.32 within author; s05). A task whose tests collapse usually keeps a high judge:
   121	    - d9e08524: 2.88 / 94.74, final 48.81
   122	    - 8eae0f87: 6.54 / 91.49, final 49.02
   123	    - 5 of the 18 tasks below 40 still had judge >= 60, and each needed tests <= 11.
   124	  - Our gate runs show the mirror image: probe band rubric 0-25 but tests 73-85, best 40.48.
   125	  - Legality: S2/G5 plus J2, each already legal.
   126	  - Proof: on frozen QC-passed bytes, 1 valid run with tests <= 60 and rubric <= 20, and 3 fresh blind reads with tests <= 60, losses WRONG or v3.5 hidden-scale.
   127	- **N2. Held-out weight-5 share of at least 50% (the dial for L2).**
   128	  - Evidence: 8 tasks at or above 50%: mean final 34.8, tests median about 7, 5 below 40 (cur90: 9 tasks, mean 32.8, 6 below 40). It is the strongest single predictor (within-author r_tests -0.43).
   129	  - Caveats: n = 8, 3 from one author, 1 hole task.
   130	  - Apply: G3 Shape D with at least 6 hidden corpora at w5.
   131	  - Proof: 2 of 3 blind reads lose at least 40% of positive test weight on the held-out tier while passing the shipped-data checks.
   132	- **N3. Small positive judge total (WEAK, do not design for it).** The lowest judge halves come from 4-9 positive criteria (725e575c jw 12 → -25.0; 42e79476 jw 16 → -6.25). One criterion is then worth 8-25 judge points, which raises variance. Note it when reading a low judge.
   133	
   134	Under-weighted by the doc, already in our rules: P-5 probe band (judge), P-3 hidden larger instances (42e79476 is our dispatch at 14.7), and the S3 unique-fit habit (18b5d99f).
   135	
   136	## 5. Gate < 40 recommendation
   137	- Arithmetic: final < 40 means tests + rubric < 80 (s08 O4). At our gate-run test levels (73-85), the rubric would have to be 7 or below, down to -5, which a legal judge does not reach (the probe band gives 0-25). Our 10 valid gate runs: 1 below 40 (dispatch 14.7, tests 35.64), 4 below 50, mean tests 78.7, mean rubric 23.5.
   138	- Honest < 40 shapes in Final_Delivery: 18 tasks, 15 after removing hole tasks. Tests median 9.36, judge median 35.51; 17 of 18 have tests < 85 and judge < 85. Exception: 725e575c (tests 96.55, judge -25.0 from a 12-point judge with one fired negative). Two routes:
   139	  - (a) Held-out collapse: tests <= 11 with judge 15-74 (8defd7be, 59417607, 18b5d99f, 9f5486ac, 80202e15).
   140	  - (b) Mid tests with a crushed judge: 5b2b0901 36.56/6.98, b5c7b14c 54.64/8.57, b51a883e 62.5/15.79.
   141	- Recommendation:
   142	  - Keep tests < 85 as a side condition. It is the only one still binding: it blocks the "tests high, negatives push the judge below zero" route seen in 725e575c.
   143	  - Rubric < 85 is implied by final < 40 (rubric 85 would need tests < -5) and can be dropped as redundant. Keeping it costs nothing.
   144	  - The working design target should be **tests <= 60 with rubric <= 20** (N1). Any tests figure of 65 or more needs rubric <= 15 and leaves no variance margin (±10 final).
   145	  - Raise v3.6's first-write aim from tests <= 75 to tests <= 60, and the blind bar from <= 80 to <= 65.
   146	
   147	## 6. What is new vs our prior studies
   148	Studies compared:
   149	- delivery_study (21 tasks, `synthesis_6c6fcf3/DELIVERY_LEARNINGS.md`)
   150	- delivery_study2 (19 tasks, g1-g4 + `synthesis_720e1d7/SUMMARY.md`)
   151	- peer_levers G1-G5 (summaries read)
   152	- hardness_notes + `verify_ec452c9` (114-claim check of HOW_TO_MAKE_HARD_1/2)
   153	- trajectory_hardening/research_cb612aa (TRIP method)
   154	
   155	Already known: unseen inputs × whole-unit exactness drive separation (DL:47-56 TD1-TD3 = doc L2+L4), the degenerate shipped instance (S2), the probe band (SUMMARY item 3), honesty negatives over figure criteria (item 4), wrong-reading test negatives never fire (DL:54 TD8; doc's 2 of 525), variance ±20 (G13), and the hole tasks.
   156	
   157	New here:
   158	- (1) An 85-task, per-check quantification (weight 1/3/5 failure rates; within-task shipped vs held-out contrasts).
   159	- (2) Tests/judge anti-correlation (-0.40) as the cause of the ceiling.
   160	- (3) Author explains 36% of final variance; L1 weakens under that control.
   161	- (4) The held-out w5 share threshold (N2).
   162	- (5) Our probe-band tasks hold 4 of the 10 lowest judge halves in the delivered set, independent confirmation of P-5.
   163	- (6) The doc set includes 2 opus-5-5 runs.
   164	- (7) A ±40 tests gap between our caldermoor registry run and its Final_Delivery report (bytes UNVERIFIED).
   165	
   166	Peer_levers G4 found the losses in 2 of its tasks came from an ambiguous definition or undefined keys, not stated rules. So delivered low scores are not all honest, which the doc assumes.
