    57	## 6. Probe gate and evidence rules (Ayush decisions 7, 8, 11; kill rule 26 Oct)
    58	- [v3: P2 design-stage blind read, our 3-minute transliterations, registry/tasks.json:707-734] Design-stage blind read: before the full build, one P13 session reads only the draft instruction.md and the rule register with a small shipped sample and writes its program. If that program matches the oracle on the shipped sample AND on 3 hidden seeds, the design is redone before the full build.
    59	- Blind read before every probe: 3 fresh P13 blind-solve sessions (each sees only a copy of instruction.md and environment/). Score each program with the real tests and `tools/loss.py`. A rule or lever counts only when at least 2 of the 3 programs get it wrong.
    60	- [v3: new] Blind judge estimate. After its program and outputs are final, each blind session receives judge.toml and marks every criterion PASS, FAIL or UNSURE, citing the step or file that shows it (P13). The master computes, per session:
    61	  - judge lower bound = (points of PASS criteria, probes counted PASS only when the blind CHECKS log shows the exact act) minus (fired negatives) over positive points;
    62	  - judge upper bound = (PASS + UNSURE + every probe not contradicted by the log) over positive points; negatives counted only when shown;
    63	  - judge mid = outcome criteria as marked, probes at the peer pass rate 25% (g3/C_0b27b9dc.md:65 3 of 16; g3/C_7e0d8feb.md:41 4 of 18);
    64	  - final bounds = (blind tests% + judge bound) / 2.
    65	  Before a probe: when the lower-bound final is above 70 on 2 of 3 blind reads, harden or redesign before the probe (never park; v3.2 below); queue the probe otherwise.
    66	- Harden decisions rest on 1 real harness run plus that round's blind reads. [v3: CONFLICTS C16, Ayush D2 26 Oct] The final gate: tests < 100 AND final < 70. [v3.6: Ayush 27 Oct 22:20 "new gate is test < 85 , rubrics < 85 and overall < 50"] REPLACED: the final gate is now tests < 85 AND rubric < 85 AND final < 50 on that 1 valid run (final = (tests + rubric)/2, so final < 50 needs rubric < 100 - tests: tests 80 needs rubric < 20). [v3.7: Ayush 28 Oct "Target <40 now"] REPLACED again: the final gate is tests < 85 AND rubric < 85 AND final reward < 40 on 1 valid run of the frozen QC-passed bytes before push (v3.7, Ayush 28 Oct "Target <40 now"; was 50 under v3.6, Ayush 27 Oct 22:20; was tests < 100 AND final < 70 before). Final = (tests + rubric)/2, so final < 40 needs rubric < 80 - tests; design for tests <= 60 and rubric <= 20. Tasks that met the old gate and miss the new one are hardened from their trajectory (KNOWLEDGE section T) with the proven levers (1C) and the QC-safe edits; judge target is a probe band with predicted mid 15-20. [v3.4: Ayush 27 Oct 17:17 "push needs only 1 run that is QC passed and under our gate score"] Push needs 1 valid harness run on the frozen QC-passed bytes (tree sha recorded at freeze) that meets the gate; any change after that run voids it. [v3.1: QL Sugam 26 Oct 18:55 answered "no" to "is a task deliverable with tests 100 and final < 70 via the rubric"; Ayush D2 reverted] A judge-only rebuild never rescues a tests-100 task; at least one positive test must be lost.
