    71	- [v3.4: Ayush decisions 1, 5, 6, 8; 27 Oct] Order and run use. Design -> build (with precheck self-checks) -> 3 fresh blind reads -> one full QC with fix-all -> QC recheck rounds -> freeze -> 1 harness run. No hardening after a QC pass. If the run misses the gate, never re-run the same bytes (same-bytes spread is about ±17.5 tests and ±20 final, sentinel attempts 5/6); the master first writes the trajectory read-out (KNOWLEDGE.md section T: TRIP table, why it scored, QC-safe edits), then a fix prompt, then QC recheck, then 1 new run. `harbor trials regrade` of a saved run is a diagnostic Ayush may run; it is never push evidence and never packaged. [v3.7 regrade exception, Ayush 28 Oct Q1] A regrade counts as push evidence only when the edit touches judge files only (no tests/, no instruction, no environment), the run was valid, Ayush wrote OK for this regrade (verbatim in decisions.jsonl), and the regraded run is repackaged with `master_chat_tasks/tools/repackage_one.py` (A4). Otherwise diagnostic only, never packaged.
