    41	## Metadata truth
    42	
    43	- AL-7 No unearned claims: every number or claim presented as measured (scores, solve rates, "oracle scores 1.0", timing ladders) must be plausible and marked for what it is. A "Measured scores" block that is template residue - identical wording/numbers to sibling bundles, or claims about runs that produce files not in this bundle - is a fail.
    44	- AL-8 Difficulty honesty: the time estimates must be consistent with the actual task content. A task whose full solution is derivable from shipped examples in minutes cannot claim "8 hours expert". Judge the work: what must an expert actually derive, how much of it is shielded from shortcut. If the claim is implausible, fail and explain. There is no `difficulty` key in task.toml.
