    55	- TS-29 Checks never raise. Any exception inside a check aborts the whole rewardkit run, so no reward is written and an agent output that merely breaks one check turns into a verifier error instead of a score. Every read of agent output (open, parse, index, convert, subprocess) is guarded so bad, missing or hostile output makes the check return False; a negative check returns False unless the cheat is positively seen. Each check returns a bool, never a number, None or a string. Nothing at module level does work beyond defining constants, checks and registrations, because rewardkit imports the module. Trace each check against an empty workspace and against garbage in every artifact.
