+# Ten candidate tasks, ranked for a final below 35
+
+**Ranking is INFERRED, not a forecast.** Chance is a subjective prebuild estimate, cost is person-days to a QC-ready bundle, and the last column is chance divided by cost. No idea has been built or blind-tested here. Rank is for choosing a *design pilot*, not for declaring a task hard. The current gate is tests <85, rubric <85, final <40, with the design aim tests <=60, rubric <=20 (`master_chat_tasks/knowledge/LEVER_RULES_v3.md:85-91,224-228`). Source analogies are in `SOURCES.md`.
+
+| Rank | Task idea and domain | Agent deliverable and hardness mechanism | Plausible first program that is **WRONG** on valid hidden inputs | QC-clean contract and oracle | Design-blind kill condition | Chance / cost / heuristic |
+|---:|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | **Rolling reservations** (inventory ledger) | Build a rerunnable reservation engine from an event stream. Each event can reserve, partially fulfil, expire, reverse, or transfer a named lot; later availability reads the carried state. Hidden histories interleave those events at scale. Stateful stream plus hidden exact snapshots. `SOURCES.md` 7, 9, 13. | A reasonable aggregate-by-item implementation nets quantities before expiry or reversal, so it produces plausible totals but allocates the wrong lot to a later request. Shipped history has no interleaving that separates the methods. | State-transition order, tie-break, reversals, bounds, and output schema stated in input docs; hidden generator creates only valid events. Independent event-by-event oracle plus per-event invariant and mutants for changed order. No instruction supplies the algorithm. | A design-blind solver implements event order and passes 3 distinct interleaved seeds with no wrong document; reject. | 55% / 3 d / 18.3 |
+| 2 | **Parametric network repair** (communications) | Produce an exact minimum-cost set of link upgrades satisfying reachability under each hidden scenario; upgrades have shared capacity and scenario-specific failures. Hidden instances change the optimum. Exact optimization plus whole-plan grading. `SOURCES.md` 8, 13. | Greedy lowest-cost upgrades or independent per-scenario optima are feasible on shipped data but nonoptimal when one upgrade helps two scenarios and another consumes a shared capacity. | State objective, constraints, candidate set, tie-break and runtime, without solution method. Cross-check a reference integer-program formulation against a separate exhaustive solver on small cases; generated scenarios obey bounds. | A generic solver or blind program finds exact optima inside budget on 3 hidden seeds; reject or enlarge only within the published bounds and verifier margin. | 50% / 3 d / 16.7 |
+| 3 | **Backdated entitlement replay** (billing) | Compute exact invoices after backdated corrections that alter future entitlement and carry-forward credits. Hidden histories combine corrections with expiry and transfer. `SOURCES.md` 7, 9. | A forward-only program adjusts the corrected invoice but does not replay all downstream credits, producing balanced totals yet wrong customer rows. | All replay, rounding, and authority rules explicit; exact-decimal oracle; hidden seeds have a planted later divergence and rule-to-test map. | Blind solver already replays correctly on 3 seeded histories and scores >65 tests; reject. | 45% / 3 d / 15.0 |
+| 4 | **Evidence-constrained calibration** (instrumentation) | From finite published candidate sensor models, select the unique model matching all calibration observations, then process fresh hidden readings. Hidden instances change the uniquely fitting model. Bounded induction plus generalization. `SOURCES.md` 10. | First-fit or least-squares on the shipped simple points selects a plausible candidate; hidden witness separates it, making all transformed readings wrong. | List the entire hypothesis space and exact match rule; each shipped and hidden instance includes a witness proving exactly one candidate. `UNIQUENESS` proof enumerates all candidates; no unstated function family. | A design blind enumerates all candidates and passes all 3 hidden seeds; reject, as the local tariff pilot did (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:58,77-83`). | 40% / 3 d / 13.3 |
+| 5 | **Cross-source effective-date merge** (compliance register) | Build a report from revisions, revocations, and source-specific effective dates, where each field class has a different stated authority order. Hidden cases combine a revocation with a later effective date. `SOURCES.md` 9. | A single global latest-record-wins merge produces a coherent report yet uses the wrong governing value for two classes. | Provide one explicit precedence table per field class, source applicability, and tie-break; plant separating shipped facts for any rule inferred from data. Independent oracle and adjacent-precedence mutant fixtures per AL-27 (`05_Alignment_Integrity_QC.md:38`). | All blind programs apply the per-field order and pass hidden conflicts; reject. Local rule-heavy builds leaked (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:77-84`). | 35% / 3 d / 11.7 |
+| 6 | **Coupled production schedule** (manufacturing) | Output an exact least-penalty schedule with machine setup carryover, material shelf life, and one shared maintenance window across jobs. Hidden instances couple three constraints. `SOURCES.md` 8, 13. | Earliest-deadline or per-machine planning gives a feasible but nonoptimal schedule because a setup choice changes later spoilage. | State all costs, feasible schedule rules, tie-breaks and max size; compare independent CP-SAT and brute force on small seeds; verifier headroom. | Generic CP-SAT is easy and fast on hidden bounds, or first-write program is exact on 3 seeds; reject. | 45% / 4 d / 11.3 |
+| 7 | **Multi-period water allocation** (resource planning) | Generate exact allocations across reservoirs and periods with carryover, loss, priority floors, and a terminal reserve; hidden drought patterns change optimal early choices. `SOURCES.md` 8, 13. | Greedy priority-first allocations meet local period constraints but over-allocate early, leaving an avoidable later shortage. | Publish objective, all transition equations, exact rational/decimal arithmetic and tie-break; certify hidden optima with two methods on small instances. | Blind program uses DP/LP exactly within time on all hidden seeds or failures are timeout-only outside the permitted share; reject. | 40% / 4 d / 10.0 |
+| 8 | **Paired-format archive reconciliation** (data migration) | Reconstruct canonical records from fixed-width, JSONL and correction logs with exact per-record lineage. Hidden corpora add duplicate and supersession patterns that shipped data does not trigger. `SOURCES.md` 2, 5. | A row-wise parser and last-write-wins merge passes shipped rows but attributes a correction to the wrong source record after a duplicate id and partial supersession. | State grammar, escaping, identity, precedence and lineage explicitly; separate hidden slices and mutants; no mere source-token tests. | Blind programs handle duplicate/supersession seeds exactly; reject. Breadth alone has weak local signal (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:77-84`). | 35% / 4 d / 8.8 |
+| 9 | **Checkpoint and compensation ledger** (distributed jobs) | Repair a program that reconstructs task states after crash/retry, where compensation may reverse a partially committed step and idempotence keys scope to job generation. `SOURCES.md` 7, 9. | “Latest event per job” reconstruction is coherent on shipped single-generation logs but wrong when a late retry and old compensation interleave. | Publish event semantics, idempotence scope, valid order and failure behavior; test actual program on valid unseen streams. | Three blinds transliterate the replay exactly, as cleanroom/crash recovery/batch lease did (`S5_build_method/FINDINGS.md:5-7`); reject. | 30% / 4 d / 7.5 |
+| 10 | **Hidden-instance performance lab** (numerical computation) | Implement a correct exact solver for bounded subset-like dispatch decisions under a stated runtime. Hidden instance families force algorithm choice. `SOURCES.md` 8, 12. | A heuristic pruning rule returns a feasible but nonoptimal certificate on a seed where a dominated-looking partial state is needed later. | State all bounds, objective, tie-break and resource limit; oracle produces certificates; kill table splits WRONG/TIMEOUT/CRASH with verifier margins per `LEVER_RULES_v3.md:85-91`. | Strong generic exact solvers pass all seeds in budget, or only unbounded timeout causes loss; reject. Local flood/cold-chain showed this risk (`S5_build_method/FINDINGS.md:5-7`). | 25% / 5 d / 5.0 |
+
+## Shared design-blind protocol
+
+1. Before authoring a full bundle, give a fresh solver only the draft instruction, copied input, and rule register. Record its first program, its own checks, and whether the submitted program returns a valid but wrong document on three seeded hidden corpora. This follows `LEVER_RULES_v3.md:230-244` and `S5_build_method/FINDINGS.md:9`.
+2. For each idea, run the strongest obvious generic solver too. If it is exact and within the published budget, the core has no measured separating power. Classify every loss as WRONG, TIMEOUT, or CRASH; only the narrow hidden-scale exception in `LEVER_RULES_v3.md:86-91` can count timeout/crash.
+3. Require a sentence or determinate shipped fact for every graded property (`05_Alignment_Integrity_QC.md:19-21,35`), a trigger fixture for every precedence/tie rule (`:38`), and distinct observables for each rewarded check (`03_Tests_QC.md:52-55`). Never reveal the planted trap in agent-visible prose.
+4. Estimate final score from separate test and judge channels. A task that cannot plausibly reach tests <=60 and rubric <=20 is unlikely to make the current <40 gate with margin (`LEVER_RULES_v3.md:85-91`); no idea above has a verified score prediction.
